<figure class="r54-move" data-r54-move aria-labelledby="r54-move-title">
 <figcaption id="r54-move-title"><span>Figure 2</span> Copying a shop does not give it a second writer</figcaption>
 <p class="note">Application-managed drill · shop 20 · revision counts scratch operations, not price changes</p>
 <div class="nodes"><div><p class="node-title">Source B</p><p data-live data-source></p><strong data-live data-source-mode></strong></div><div><p class="node-title">Target A</p><p data-live data-target></p><strong data-live data-target-mode></strong></div></div>
 <p class="gate" data-live data-gate></p>
 <p class="explanation" data-live data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <div class="controls"><div class="buttons"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step aria-label="Step"></span></div><div data-hold class="hold" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div></div>
 <details><summary>The complete handover, as text</summary><p>The first copy has revision 0. B accepts one operation, then an in-flight operation reaches revision 2 while holding the ownership row lock. The fence waits for that transaction. A racing writer waits behind the fence and is refused afterwards. With B inactive, the final revision and both accepted operation identifiers are copied to inactive A and compared. A is activated at epoch 2. A new operation reaches revision 3; retrying an already accepted identifier leaves it at 3. B continues to refuse the old epoch. This protocol depends on every runtime write taking the ownership lock.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
 import {stepper} from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
 document.querySelectorAll('[data-r54-move]').forEach(root=>stepper(root,{steps:()=>6,draw:n=>{
  const states=[
   ['Revision 0 · epoch 1','Accepting writes','Revision 0 · epoch 2','Inactive copy','Initial copy complete; handover has not happened.','The two copies agree now. Only B accepts runtime writes. A is deliberately inactive, so agreement cannot be mistaken for permission to serve writes.'],
   ['Revision 1 · epoch 1','Accepting writes','Revision 0 · epoch 2','Inactive copy','The initial copy is already behind.','An accepted operation changes B to revision 1. The copy is a starting point; it does not include later commits automatically.'],
   ['Revision 2, uncommitted','Fence waiting for writer','Revision 0 · epoch 2','Inactive copy','The ownership lock orders the writer before the fence.','An in-flight operation holds the ownership row lock until commit. The fence waits. A racing writer queues as well; it cannot skip the same guard.'],
   ['Revision 2 · epoch 2','Fenced: writes refused','Revision 2 · epoch 2','Inactive, checked copy','Both accepted operation identifiers now match.','The in-flight transaction commits, then the fence closes B. The racing writer is refused. The final source state and retry journal are copied and compared while A remains inactive.'],
   ['Revision 2 · epoch 2','Fenced: writes refused','Revision 3 · epoch 2','Accepting writes','A accepts the next operation under epoch 2.','Only after the check does the target become writable. Requests routed with B’s old epoch are refused, even if their routing cache has not refreshed.'],
   ['Revision 2 · epoch 2','Fenced: writes refused','Revision 3 · epoch 2','Accepting writes','Retrying an accepted operation leaves revision 3.','The retry journal moved with the shop. A recognises the already accepted identifier and does not apply it again. Retaining the source fence prevents an old route from creating a competing history.']
  ][n];
  ['source','source-mode','target','target-mode','gate','explanation'].forEach((key,i)=>root.querySelector('[data-'+key+']').textContent=states[i]);
 }}));
</script>
